<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="energy_asset_realloc::capital_inflows_oil" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in net cross‑border inflows expands available foreign equity and syndicated debt, enabling sponsors and banks to fund or complete upstream and midstream oil investments and thereby raising capital directed to the oil sector.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_asset_realloc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid cross‑border outflows reduce liquidity for banks, defence contractors and intermediary financiers and constrain donor governments' ability to bridge payments, causing delays or reductions in weapons deliveries to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger net cross-border capital inflows directly increase available venture, private equity and infrastructure financing as well as cross‑border M&amp;A liquidity, boosting the rate of capital deployment into AI companies and projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="us_iran_confront::international_clearing_a" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sudden net outflows reduce correspondent-bank liquidity and raise perceived counterparty risk, prompting international banks to curtail or suspend clearing and payment services to regionally linked/sanction‑exposed banks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
