<edge source="global_bond_repricing::market_volatility" target="energy_asset_realloc::oil_export_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in market volatility raise price and counterparty risk, leading traders and buyers to reduce spot purchases and shippers to delay loadings, which curtails short‑term crude export volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_asset_realloc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::market_volatility" target="russia_ukraine_war::defensive_posture_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp spikes in cross‑market volatility raise near‑term risk perceptions among governments and militaries, prompting precautionary increases in readiness, forward presence and deployments to deter opportunistic escalation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::market_volatility" target="us_china_tech_trade::regulatory_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">1</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute spikes in market volatility spur regulatory and political pressure to shore up strategic sectors, prompting quicker imposition or tightening of export controls, investment screens, and tech oversight aimed at stabilizing markets and protecting domestic capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::market_volatility" target="us_iran_confront::shipping_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp increases in fixed‑income and FX volatility raise war‑risk and insurance premia and trigger risk‑averse ship operators and charterers to divert or delay sailings through high‑risk regional lanes, lowering commercial throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
