<edge source="global_bond_repricing::auction_clearing_yield" target="energy_asset_realloc::access_agreements_extent" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher auction clearing yields increase sovereign borrowing costs and fiscal pressure, prompting authorities to seek upfront revenue and inward investment by accelerating or expanding long‑term access agreements, concessions, or asset‑sale arrangements with external parties.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_asset_realloc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::auction_clearing_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher auction clearing yields raise immediate borrowing costs for sovereigns and state export‑credit agencies, shrinking budgetary headroom and the willingness to finance large or expedited arms procurements and export credits, slowing transfer tempo.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
