  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Expansion of long‑term access contracts between the conflict state and third‑party energy partners creates economic interdependence and carve‑outs that split allies' economic and political incentives, reducing willingness to sustain coordinated military planning and burden‑sharing.</data>
