<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::oil_export_volume" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased crude export volumes raise near‑term fiscal and foreign‑exchange receipts that are fungible for fuel, munitions, contracted logistics and mercenary/contractor services, enabling higher sustained rates and scale of offensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::oil_export_volume" target="us_china_tech_trade::geo_competition" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher oil export flows to a major buyer reduce that buyer's urgency to secure alternative suppliers or strategic footholds, thereby lowering immediate interstate competition intensity over energy and related tech partnerships.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
