<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter sanction enforcement raises counterparty, correspondent‑bank and secondary‑sanctions risk, causing foreign banks and investors to curtail lending, portfolio placements and FX settlement with the jurisdiction, directly reducing net cross‑border capital inflows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="global_bond_repricing::auction_clearing_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher intensity of sanctions narrows the eligible investor base and increases required risk premia for remaining bidders, forcing sovereign debt auctions to clear at higher yields to attract demand.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, more comprehensive enforcement of trade, financial and asset restrictions severs procurement channels, payment rails and logistics used to buy and ship weapons and critical components, reducing the tempo and volume of transfers to front‑line users.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharper enforcement of sanctions on energy actors raises counterparty and payment‑risk for banks and VCs, prompting them to cut or delay cross‑border AI funding and FDI into counterparties tied to sanctioned jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="us_china_tech_trade::chip_production_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Targeted sanctions and tighter enforcement disrupt payment flows and spare‑parts shipments for fabs that rely on suppliers linked to sanctioned energy firms, forcing temporary slowdown or idling of production lines.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="us_iran_confront::international_clearing_a" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharper and more aggressive sanction enforcement causes correspondent banks and payment processors to cut or block transactions with targeted actors, directly degrading their access to global interbank clearing and payment rails.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_asset_realloc::sanction_enforcement_lev" target="us_iran_confront::shipping_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased enforcement raises legal and insurance risks for commercial shippers and charterers, prompting carriers to avoid regional ports and routes and thereby reducing maritime cargo throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_asset_realloc</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
